# Never commit personal data exports
*.zip
Basic_LinkedInDataExport*

# Never commit RAW camera originals into public/. Two reasons: they are huge
# (one batch was 319 MB) and, because this repo is public, anything committed
# stays readable in git history forever even after deletion — including EXIF
# GPS. Process them into web assets FIRST:
#   node scripts/process-community-media.mjs <slug> <prefix> --from <raw dir>
# Processed assets are named <prefix>-01.jpg / <prefix>-video-01.mp4, so they
# are unaffected by these patterns. Keep raws outside the repo (or in /tmp).
public/images/**/*.[Hh][Ee][Ii][Cc]
public/images/**/*.[Hh][Ee][Ii][Ff]
public/images/**/*.[Mm][Oo][Vv]
public/images/**/*.[Tt][Ii][Ff]
public/images/**/*.[Tt][Ii][Ff][Ff]
public/images/**/IMG_*
public/images/**/DSC_*
public/images/**/DCIM*
public/images/**/100_*

# Local-only verification harnesses (Playwright; needs `npm i --no-save playwright`)
verify-*.mjs
diag.mjs

